Mastering every stage of the technological tree as a lone human requires a meticulous, hyper-focused integration of earth sciences, physics, and patience. [1] 
------------------------------
## Phase 1: The Primitive Era (Tools From Stone)
Before manipulating energy, you must manipulate mass to create mechanical leverage. [2, 3] 

* 
* Flint Knapping: Source high-silica rocks like flint, chert, or obsidian. Strike the edges at a 45-degree angle with a heavy river cobblestone (percussive flaking). Use a piece of deer antler to pressure-flake the edges, shaving microscopic layers to achieve a scalpel-like sharpness. [4] 
* The Hand Axe: Shape a pear-sized stone so it features a wide, weighted rear base for your palm and a razor-thin, uniform edge at the front. This is your master tool for carving wood, scraping animal hides, and processing fibers.
* Cordage Manufacturing: Harvest wild flax, stinging nettle, or the inner bark of willow trees. Dry the stalks, crush them to separate the inner fibers, and use a "reverse-twist" technique (twisting two strands clockwise while wrapping them counter-clockwise around each other) to make high-tensile rope.
* 

