## Phase 2: Pyrotechnics (Controlling Energy)
Fire unlocks chemical modification, advanced preservation, and massive caloric availability. [5, 6] 

* 
* The Bow Drill: Carve a straight, hard-wood spindle and a flat, soft-wood hearth board. Cut a small V-shaped notch on the edge of the hearth board directly beneath where your spindle will spin. Use your bow and cordage to spin the spindle rapidly against the board, channeling frictional heat down into a pile of sawdust until it glows as an independent ember.
* Charcoal Harvesting: Dig a pit, stack hardwood logs inside, and ignite them. Once burning intensely, seal the pit completely with mud and turf to cut off oxygen. The wood will undergo pyrolysis, burning off water vapor, sap, and volatile gases, leaving behind pure carbon blocks that burn twice as hot as raw wood. [7, 8] 
* 

